@startuml
title 🎯 Test Strategy: Heuristic vs Fuzzing (Oracle-Guided)

skinparam style strictuml
skinparam ParticipantPadding 20
skinparam BoxPadding 10

box "Heuristic Test" #LightBlue
  actor TesterH as "👤 Tester"
  participant HI as "📚 HeuristicInputs"
  participant OracleH as "🧠 Oracle"
  participant SystemH as "🌐 Form System"
end box

box "Fuzzing Test" #LightGray
  actor TesterF as "👤 Tester"
  participant BaseF as "🧪 BaseInputs"
  participant MutatorF as "🔀 Mutator"
  participant OracleF as "🧠 Oracle"
  participant SystemF as "🌐 Form System"
  participant ReportF as "📊 Report Engine"
end box

' --- Heuristic Test ---
TesterH -> HI : Definisce input (valid, invalid, edge)
HI -> OracleH : Calcola predizione
OracleH -> SystemH : Esegue test form
SystemH --> OracleH : Risultato (esito, validazione)
OracleH -> TesterH : Confronto predizione ↔ risultato

' --- Fuzzing Test ---
TesterF -> BaseF : Sceglie input base (es. "bob")
BaseF -> MutatorF : Applica mutazioni semantiche
MutatorF -> OracleF : Predice esito atteso
MutatorF -> SystemF : Esegue input mutato sul form
SystemF --> OracleF : Risultato osservato
OracleF -> ReportF : Valuta accuratezza oracolo
SystemF -> ReportF : Log di performance, anomalie
ReportF --> TesterF : Genera dashboard/coverage
@enduml